tool.description:
Compile and run bounded C# on the trusted workstation. read reports; preview rolls back; apply requires fresh host authorization and readback. In code mode print text(result): do not assume result.content or stringify rendered text. Inspect failure/diagnostics before correcting source. PROGRAM_PARTIAL_OUTPUT is unverified failed-program output. Snapshot/graph repair uses exact retained lineage (five attempts); committed_verified checkpoints allow up to64 verified steps. Leave operation_budget at default normally: operation_budget:1 limits dependent effects, not one intended target; constrain the graph instead. Native programs use explicit scope below. Certified-only exposure remains fail-closed.

Optional native_program (development/laboratory, Revit2024 only): use when a useful read or write needs Autodesk.Revit.DB APIs unavailable in the snapshot/graph SDK. Same agent, local compiler process, then authenticated Revit execution; no AI handoff. Set native_program.entry_type to the full C# class name containing public static string Execute(Autodesk.Revit.DB.Document doc). mode:"read" opens no transaction and must be nonmutating; filter/aggregate in code and return concise string/JSON (max32768characters). For example a FilteredElementCollector(doc).OfCategory(BuiltInCategory.OST_MEPSpaces).WhereElementIsNotElementType() can filter names and count missing values without shipping every room to the model. Report precisely what document/category/filter was inspected; returned prose/counts never automatically establish exhaustive source coverage.
mode:"apply" uses one host-owned atomic transaction group, without a separate preview call. For general native-code work explicitly set native_program.effect_scope="active_document"; omit allowed_existing_unique_ids, allow_create and max_affected_elements. Authorization remains bound to this current document and exact source. Do not predict Revit-dependent IDs: the host records actual changes, enforces pinned/grouped protection and a4096-ID audit-capacity bound, and independently verifies commit/rollback. That audit is not task success. Verify the requested geometry/values/connections and saved persistence as applicable; use code-and-result review against original user intent for unrelated work. Review should inspect exact source plus native outcomes, not guess all downstream changes. Legacy listed_elements scope retains declared existing UniqueIds/create permission/1..64affected budget. Creating new elements can also modify existing dependents; an empty legacy target set is a constraint, not permission. Do not blindly whitelist errors or replay an uncertain operation. Unknown effects require reconciliation. No nested transactions, document open/close/save/export, external IO, reflection, asynchronous code or lifecycle operations. Use existing save/file-inspection tools afterward. deadline_ms250..10000 is cooperative: it cannot interrupt a blocking Revit API call. The host binds source/assembly/current document/session/revision and exact references; it rejects stale scope and settles rollback/unknown effects. Omit snapshot/category/parameters/operation_budget/result_reference/resume/continue_from_checkpoint on this lane. Compiler success is not native execution; native commit is not task verification. Inspect native_outcome, independently read back intended values/relationships, and review rendered placement when relevant. No automatic retry after an uncertain write. Select bounded native_outcome.program_result from the canonical observation for delivery; task correctness remains evidence-dependent.

Two explicit C# lanes share this tool and the same reasoning agent. Default snapshot/graph lane: exactly one public IDynamicRevitProgram implementation with DynamicProgramResult Execute(DynamicRevitContext c), using RevitOperator.DynamicRevitSdk. This default runs outside Revit with DTOs, not Autodesk.Revit.DB/doc/Document or Python. The optional native_program lane below instead compiles against actual Revit metadata and executes on Revit's main thread. No filesystem, network, processes, reflection, or dynamic binding in either lane. No shell or local SDK search is needed.
Basic SDK: c.Input.Coverage has SourceScope (active_document_non_type_elements), Category, ParameterNames, Limit, ReturnedCount and HasMore. HasMore=true means the native enumeration was truncated; filter/aggregate results then describe only that partial snapshot. Null coverage on an older SDK means unknown enumeration completeness. HasMore=false covers only the requested active-document category, not linked models or parameter availability. Count missing/null requested fields separately. Filter and aggregate inside C# before returning bounded report entries, instead of emitting every input row. c.Input.Document has Title, ProjectFingerprint, SessionId, ActiveViewName. c.Elements is IReadOnlyList<DynamicElementDto>: UniqueId:string, ElementId:long, Category:string, FamilyName/TypeName:string?, Parameters:Dictionary<string,string?>, WritableParameters:string[], Location:DynamicPointDto? (X,Y,Z in feet), IsPinned/IsGrouped:bool. c.Report(string key,string value) retains up to 64 entries (key<=128,value<=1024); c.Log(string) retains up to 64 bounded lines; return c.Complete(). LINQ and ordinary deterministic C# algorithms are supported. Only when edits are authorized: c.Plan.MoveElement(element,xFeet,yFeet,zFeet), c.Plan.SetParameter(element,parameter,value). Report-only programs must leave the graph empty. Set category=OST_DuctCurves and snapshot_limit=20 for a bounded duct sample; do not call the sample a census.
Working report example:
using System;
using System.Linq;
using RevitOperator.DynamicRevitSdk;
public sealed class SampleReport : IDynamicRevitProgram {
  public DynamicProgramResult Execute(DynamicRevitContext c) {
    c.Report("Inspected", c.Elements.Count.ToString());
    foreach (var group in c.Elements.GroupBy(e => e.TypeName ?? "(unnamed)"))
      c.Report("Type: " + group.Key, group.Count().ToString());
    c.Report("Limit", "Bounded snapshot sample; not a complete model inventory.");
    return c.Complete();
  }
}
Use mode:"read" for reports. snapshot_limit is 1..4096 for read and 1..1000 for preview/apply (default 200). A snapshot covers active-document non-type elements, optionally restricted to one category; it excludes linked documents. Check c.Input.Coverage.HasMore and count missing requested parameter values before claiming an exhaustive answer. Establish the total cohort and coverage before claiming a census. Missing parameter keys do not establish missing model relationships: use actual schedule fields or a supported relationship query for Room/Space associations, and state what was not available. Omit optional time limits normally; worker_deadline_ms is 1000..30000 and apply_deadline_ms is 100..5000. operation_budget is 1..256 even for an empty report graph; it also caps native affected elements, including Revit's dependent changes. The successful raw tool payload contains report and logs at its root. For canonical result delivery select concise scalar resultItems such as path:["report","Inspected"] from the returned Observation ID, without adding a payload wrapper. For audits or gap lists, include a prioritized assessment with evidence_indices referencing those resultItems, limits, and up to three useful outside-input questions. Do not select the entire report object for an assessment; the structured delivery itself becomes the final answer.

Advanced MEP/annotation result-reference graphs: retrieve tool.inputSchema.properties.source for the complete SDK contract before using that lane.

