Advanced: IDynamicResultReferenceRevitProgramV1 uses result_reference, c.Fact(...), c.TraceStep(...), c.Require(...), c.NeedFacts(...) or c.Complete(). Use its exact domain contract before composing MEP/annotation graphs.
For several known existing MEP joins, use one result-reference MEP graph rather than one program per edge. DynamicMepResultReferenceBuilderV1.ConnectMep(builder, externalTargets, resultReferences, connectorA, connectorB) adds one pair; repeat for the bounded independent pairs. Each node requires exactly two total targets. Existing owners use trusted DynamicExternalTargetReferenceV1 facts; a curve created earlier in this graph uses that handle's Reference("curve"), which adds its dependency. DynamicMepConnectorSelectorV1 contains SourceIdentityHash, NativeConnectorId, ExpectedOriginFeet, ExpectedDomain and ExpectedShape; derive these from exact authenticated facts/SDK identities, never fabricate identity hashes or substitute connector enumeration order. Native connector ID zero is valid. Preserve exact sizes and physically open compatible endpoints in the plan. Use c.TraceStep and c.Require to bind intended edges to observed facts, then c.Complete().
The implemented MEP graph vocabulary is create_mep_curve, set_mep_curve_size, connect_mep, create_elbow_fitting and create_transition_fitting. Family placement is not activated in this graph: place and verify families with the existing typed placement tool, then batch their known connections. One graph uses one primitive family, so MEP plus annotation requires separate verified steps. The host observes one bound document/session/revision, executes rollback preview, issues fresh one-use authorization, and applies a group of node transactions with effect/topology/readback checks. A failed group is not a set of successful siblings; treat unknown outcomes as unresolved and use retained reconciliation. An apply call includes internal preview/authorization/native calls and is not a single unguarded ConnectTo loop. The result_reference selector and effect_budget must bind the actual document, exact targets and bounded collateral effects; this brief guide is not permission to invent the required hashes. Repair a compile error with changed source and resume:{prior_run_id,prior_evidence_sha256,mode:"repair"}; five attempts share one evidence-bound loop.
